  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116304",
      "title": "Getting Started with Angular's Http Client",
      "lectureOrder": 222,
      "videoOrder": 212,
      "sourceHash": "be0f6766074b3f83a83022c4c10e486469693576131ca0117df28799259ec79e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 2.58,
          "en": "So let's fetch some data from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "And for that, here in my Angular application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 9.1,
          "en": "I'll go to the available places component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.08,
          "end": 12.6,
          "en": "because I wanna work on those available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.6,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "and populate this box with that backend data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 21,
          "en": "So this component is the right place to fetch that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "You could also use a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 25.53,
          "en": "and that is something we'll switch to later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.53,
          "end": 27.993,
          "en": "But for now, let's work in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 31.08,
          "en": "And the question therefore is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.08,
          "end": 36.08,
          "en": "how do we send HTTP requests in Angular applications?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 42.44,
          "en": "And the answer is a special service you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "which you can inject into your Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 48,
          "en": "or into your services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "It's the HTTP client, which I will inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.523,
          "en": "by using the inject function from Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "And then it's the HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 62.9,
          "en": "imported from at Angular slash common slash http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 68.1,
          "en": "So that is a service in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.1,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "that is provided by Angular that helps us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 74.13,
          "en": "with sending HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 76.803,
          "en": "and managing their responses and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 82.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now, if you would try to inject it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 87.71000000000001,
          "en": "you'd get an error here in your browser developer tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "A null injector error that Angular actually does know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 96.483,
          "en": "how to provide such an HTTP client value to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.53,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "Because in this application, we never set up a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.25,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "for this service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "And as you learned before in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.13,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "you need to tell Angular how to provide the things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 110.58,
          "en": "that you later want to inject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "And this HTTP client thing is not something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "that would be available in all Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 118.023,
          "en": "out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 120.75,
          "en": "Instead to be provided,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.75,
          "end": 125.253,
          "en": "you could add the provider's array here in your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.45,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "But typically, you wanna use the HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "in other parts of the application as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "And therefore, it's more common to be provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 140.78,
          "en": "right in the main.ts file or if you're using modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 143.553,
          "en": "to provide it in the root module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "Now, if you're not using modules, then you would provide it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "by adding a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "to this bootstrap application function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 157.29,
          "en": "And then there, you can add the providers setting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.29,
          "end": 160.5,
          "en": "which takes an array of providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 164.403,
          "en": "to register a provider for this HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "And you register that provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "by calling the provide HTTP client function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "which must be imported from at Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 177.513,
          "en": "slash common slash HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.98,
          "en": "By executing this function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.98,
          "end": 185.61,
          "en": "you set up such a HTTP client provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.61,
          "end": 188.85,
          "en": "and that is a function that's provided by Angular of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "so all you have to do is call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 194.82,
          "en": "And then you'll have such a HTTP client provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "registered application wide if you do it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.93,
          "end": 201.66,
          "en": "and therefore, now you'll see the error is gone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.66,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "if you reload the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "Because now with that provider added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 209.43,
          "en": "application wide in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 213.813,
          "en": "Angular knows how to inject such a HTTP client service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 219.86,
          "en": "So that's how you set it up and make it ready for usage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "Of course, you could also inject it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "by using the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 229.44,
          "en": "As always, you can inject anything here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 231.99,
          "en": "You don't have to use the inject function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.99,
          "end": 234.123,
          "en": "So that would be an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.44,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "And of course, you could also be using modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 241.413,
          "en": "instead of Standalone Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 246.09,
          "en": "In that case, the next lecture will contain instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.09,
          "end": 249.66,
          "en": "that shows you how you could provide the HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.66,
          "end": 251.58,
          "en": "in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.58,
          "end": 254.283,
          "en": "Here, I'll stick to Standalone Components though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "And with that, let's now use that HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 261.483,
          "en": "to send such a request.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
